    feat(gate): sweep the whole dual standard, not the half already mechanical
    
    A new Skill's conformance split in two: one half the trusted checks already
    refuse, one half an admission issue could enumerate and nothing would re-read.
    An enumeration inside an issue body is author memory, which is the defect of
    shape this repository cures everywhere else.
    
    `check_skill_bundles.py` already walks every `skills/*` directory, so the
    second half lands there rather than in a new surface. Per Skill it now
    asserts: a validator exists, is wired into its own `run_all.SKILL_CHECKS` row
    next to that Skill's test discovery, and is count-tied to its entrypoint; an
    admission stamp exists and was taken against the bytes that are here now; the
    eval campaign is a directory whose planted-negative arms do not borrow a
    positive arm's assertion; every `receipts.json` entry names its ground; both
    collection documents carry the Skill's row and kind; and the pstack birth
    triple is present by shape.
    
    The count tie is the load-bearing one, and it is generic by construction: each
    validator declares `SKILL_MD_CLAUSES`, the gate reads that tuple out of the
    validator's own bytes with `ast`, and compares it to the entrypoint's `## `
    sections. There is no per-skill list in the gate to go stale, and a hollowed
    SKILL.md reds against a tuple the hollowing never touched. Nothing is
    imported: in CI this file is trusted code reading a candidate tree as data, so
    `run_all.py` and every validator are parsed, never executed.
    
    Two nonconformances in already-admitted Skills, fixed here rather than
    grandfathered:
    
    - `context-closure-engineering`'s `task-packet-unbounded` (expected FAIL)
      named `test_context_pack_selftest_passes` -- the same assertion its POSITIVE
      case names. One execution stood for two arms, so the admission receipt
      carried a planted-negative control id whose only measurement was the
      positive control. It now has its own arm, which defuses the per-row packet
      binding and requires the tree to red.
    - Every `receipts.json` entry in `control-backup` and `control-code-intel` was
      a claim plus prose, with no ground any process re-reads. Nine and three
      entries respectively now name the driver whose selftest replays them; the
      rest carry the explicit `HOST_OBSERVED` exit, so a one-time host observation
      and a replayed claim stop looking alike in the bytes.
    
    `run_all.py` is untouched: the new assertions live behind a gate it already
    runs, and the runner's `SKILL_CHECKS` is read as data rather than edited.
    
    The Doctor of the birth triple is the stamper's refusing preflight, not the
    cadence sweep's own doctor: the sweep is N-class and no gate may name it.
    
    Each assertion has its own planted negative in
    `tests/test_repository_controls.py`, and all fifteen were also driven through
    the shipped CLI against mutated scratch trees. What this cannot prove is
    method honesty -- that the interview behind a feature map was faithful. That
    stays with campaigns, planted negatives and wave monitors, and the gate says
    so on the page.
    
    Refs ed3c/skill-concerns#74
    
